{"type": "final", "turn": 3, "content": "\n\nI've built a confidence-stratified labeling design for your run (128x128 grid = 16,384 windows, model OlmoEarth-v1-FT-AWF-Base):\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Design | `confidence`, budget **300** of 16,384 windows, 5 confidence strata (allocation 106 / 79 / 47 / 34 / 34) |\n| Population | every valid window of the map, graded on its majority class |\n| Design file | `.../B4/cluster/2/workspace/design_scores_8f3527f9_confidence_300_s0.json` |\n| Label CSV | same folder, `_to_label.csv` \u2014 holds each window's location, mapped class, and rows to fill |\n\n**Next step:** open the CSV and for each of the 300 windows set `wrong = 1` if the map's class is not what is on the ground, else `0` (optionally also the true class id for per-class accuracy). Save it back, and I'll run the estimator to return the error rate plus the interval that this design earns.\n\nNote: because this is a targeted (low-confidence-first) design, the estimate stays unbiased, but the interval must come from the estimator \u2014 a plain p \u00b1 1.96\u00b7sqrt(p(1-p)/n) would be wrong for this design.", "forced_by_turn_cap": false, "grounding_revised": false, "seq": 6, "t": 12.241, "seconds": 2.617}
